    {
      "finding": "An already-presented one-frame camera handoff was followed by skipped unchanged frames, producing an apparent 92 ms combat gap.",
      "disposition": "Classify motion from completed app updates. Already-presented movement can end at explicit idle; new movement remains chargeable until the next paint. Emit at most one interval per native gap."
    },
    {
      "finding": "The first classifier revision could hide a short movement that started and ended between paints.",
      "disposition": "Fixed after Opus 5.5 review; new pending movement remains charged through the following paint. Eight regressions cover short bursts, missing updates, completed-update timing and empty evidence."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Motion-only intervals do not establish responsiveness while actors and camera are idle.",
      "disposition": "Also enforce a 60 ms maximum combat GUI-update interval. The prior benchmark already filtered for motion; it did not demand redundant paints for every idle update."
    },
